nt upon the nothing and what he's  calling the negative behavior of the  nothing or another way that he talks  about it is a wholly repelling gesture  so we need to get at that and this is in  this section the response to the  question he tells us that in anxiety  there's this shrinking before and it's a  kind of bewildered calm it affects both  the the design of the human being the  core what it is that the human being is  in their existence and the totality of  beings that they are in  within remember that design is one being  among other beings although it's a very  special kind of being and what we saw is  that beings as a whole in anxiety are  revealed to us or reveal themselves to  us as in retreat as moving away from us  Heidegger uses these spatial metaphors  and then he talks about the nothing  itself he says the nothing does not  attract it is essentially repelling but  this is a different kind of repulsion  than we might think of in terms of like  repugnant or negative you know response  to electromagnetic stimuli or something  like that instead he's using metaphors  here too you know we don't we have to  use spatial metaphors it is it is  repelling he says this repulsion is  itself as such a parting gesture so you  know think of waving goodbye or it might  also be a parting gesture like screw you  you know or any any other sort of thing  but it is it is pushing beings away and  these beings are as he said submerging  as a whole there they're losing their  their meaning you might say and he calls  us a holy repelling gesture towards  beings that are in retreat as a whole  and he says this is the action of the  nothing that oppresses design-in anxiety  so one of the things that the action of  the nothing is is a pressing design a  pressing you know the person in how they  feel  so the nothing is is intrinsically  involved in the very feeling mood tuned  meant however we want to translate it of  anxiety that turns out to be one of the  most important moods 